{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$ is the *second derivative* of $y$. In other words, it's the derivative of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$, which is the derivative of $y$.\n\nBecause of this, we need to differentiate $y$ twice in order to find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[(3x-2)^4\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=12(3x-2)^3\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[(3x-2)^4\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=4(3x-2)^3\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}(3x-2)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=4(3x-2)^3\\cdot(3)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=12(3x-2)^3\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ to find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[12(3x-2)^3\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=108(3x-2)^2\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[12(3x-2)^3\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=12\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[(3x-2)^3\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=12\\cdot3(3x-2)^2\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}(3x-2)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=36(3x-2)^2\\cdot(3)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=108(3x-2)^2\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=108(3x-2)^2$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $y=(3x-2)^4$.\n\n**Find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$.**\n\n$\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":"0","simplify":false,"value":"108(3x-2)^{2}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"static":false,"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
